}}\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{7\\sqrt{7}}{|\\sqrt{7}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{7}x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{7}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{7}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{7}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7}{|x|\\sqrt{7{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{7\\sqrt{7}}{|\\sqrt{7}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{7}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\sqrt{7}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =7\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =7\\,\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =7\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{7}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320435 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320436 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320437 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320438 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320439 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1041 "selection" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1104 #edb/ref 17592186320435 13194139534927 true] [17592186320434 1110 #uuid "00edf96d-388d-510c-9abf-66bfe44e45fb" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320435 1034 "7\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{7}x)+C" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320435 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534927 true] [17592186320435 1111 #uuid "e7159a3d-ec8e-5f83-aa7f-107534ab4dee" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320436 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320436 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534927 true] [17592186320436 1111 #uuid "02128603-73ff-5fe6-b741-2f7c9c4e81ae" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320437 1034 "7\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{arcsec}(x)+C" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320437 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534927 true] [17592186320437 1111 #uuid "282719bf-558a-5d37-8851-6bc4de23d2fd" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320438 1034 "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{7}x)+C" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320438 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534927 true] [17592186320438 1111 #uuid "f5ca3b7e-6cbd-5c64-9a92-15c80432df71" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320439 1034 "\\text{arcsec}(7x)+C" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320439 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534927 true] [17592186320439 1111 #uuid "2c8f6ca3-0450-51c8-937b-b837efe2a41d" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320440 1017 #edb/ref 17592186320441 13194139534927 true] [17592186320440 1089 "q-114080" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320440 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534927 true] [17592186320440 1100 "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320440 1113 #uuid "5e4c70d4-0535-5065-80e6-9431b5d6608c" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320440 1145 "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (2\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =8(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320442 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320443 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320444 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320445 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320446 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1041 "selection" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1104 #edb/ref 17592186320446 13194139534927 true] [17592186320441 1110 #uuid "460d7418-1ca7-5dc3-946f-fd68dee12a65" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320442 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{8}" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320442 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534927 true] [17592186320442 1111 #uuid "20fb36d6-035a-5391-ba4f-bd9e7475c99f" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320443 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{24}" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320443 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534927 true] [17592186320443 1111 #uuid "e5599341-a5a5-5cd4-8c05-af43c4f10e5c" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320444 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" 13194139534927 true] [17592186320444 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194